16745:     "note": "*** THE ONLY SEAT THAT CAUGHT THE ROUND'S FALSE PANEL CLAIM, AND IT WAS THE SEAT BEING MISCOUNTED. *** It read the shipped comment's 'a panel of nine seats reached this 8-1', observed it was written while this seat was still running, and noted it does not vote B -- an L4 wrong record about the panel itself, inside a round about a guard nobody checked. It ALSO measured that build/gxemul's mtime moved underneath it mid-review, so its own 'pre-fix' run was post-fix and indistinguishable in the output; the round's witness was re-derived from `git show HEAD:` because of that. Further measured findings, all rebuilt in a private clone with build/ and est/ untouched: -E baresh reproduces (third machine); -e jornada690 reproduces; all five machines carry the device (IPRD=0xda74 on each); the accept coverage was ASYMMETRIC (dreamcast had frequency but no readback -- row added); the guard-only growth mutant reddens all four accept rows while every kill row stays green; and Option D works mechanically (-C SH7708R needs no rebuild, store hits non-existant paddr, banner byte-identical) but must be REJECTED because arch-3 removes the entire SH-4 register block, SH-3 interrupt handlers are /* TODO */ stubs at cpu_sh.c:527-533, and cpu_sh.c:224 uses a leftover UTLB loop counter as templ.line, inert only because that handler is a stub. Its verdict was OPTION C (B plus a synthetic clock for baresh/testsh); the B half shipped, the second half is filed as sh4testclock on the round-scope rule."
