17444:    "note": "*** CLOSED IN #458, WHICH THE ASSESS PHASE HAD RULED A SEPARATE ROUND. THE RULING WAS OVERTAKEN BY AN IMPLEMENTATION FACT, AND THE CHANGE IS RECORDED RATHER THAN MERGED QUIETLY. *** The pass-1 seat refused the merge correctly on the evidence it had -- different semantic classes, witness shapes differing in ORDER, and this row's own filing saying 'a second design question, its own round'. What that ruling could not know: rewriting priority nibbles of a table that may already hold a pending request leaves int_to_assert STALE, so the rescan is load-bearing FOR THE REGISTER FIX ITSELF. Measured corroboration: `rescanonly` builds identical to `pre` -- the rescan fixes nothing observable ALONE -- which is exactly why it cannot be deferred without leaving #458's own table able to go stale. Separable as filings, not as code.\nThe round block records this as a SCOPE CHANGE, because an earlier draft said 'sh4prioraise is NOT in this round' in the same breath as 'the rescan half IS present' and 'the row that isolates it is red on an IPR-only build'. Both were true; together they denied shipping what shipped.\nNOT CLOSED: the standing-LOWER direction. No row asserts at a high priority and then lowers it while the request stands, so a mutant guarding the rescan with `if (int_to_assert == 0)` is predicted to escape. Filed as sh4standinglower with the one-line kill row a seat supplied."
