17791-     "note": "*** THE ROW SAYS 'NOT WITNESSED', AND A WITNESS IS BOTH CONSTRUCTIBLE AND ADMISSIBLE. *** The carrier's own rule is that 'no witness of either kind' is a CHECKABLE claim and must be checked rather than asserted -- dfreq's was measured false by building one in a single session -- so this is that check, done by READING (flagged as a reading, not a measurement; the tree was busy with #461's pre-fix run and a probe would have contended with it). THE OBSERVABLE ALREADY EXISTS: cpu_sh.c:168-173 registers `iprio_%x` as a readable setting for EVERY 0x20 slot in 0..0xfff, which includes `iprio_3e0` (IRQ15). The hardwired priority loop at cpu_sh.c:390 is `for (i = SH4_INTEVT_IRQ0; i <= SH4_INTEVT_IRQ14; i += 0x20)`, so slot 0x3e0 is never written and keeps 0 while 0x3c0 (IRQ14) gets 1. Two `print` commands on an unmodified machine separate the two. AND RUNG 2 IS THE RIGHT RUNG FOR IT, not a concession: the ladder licenses machine construction as a reproduction for 'defects in code construction itself executes (init-time)', naming the macppc heap OOB #23 as the exemplar. This IS init-time -- the loop populates the priority table at CPU init and the defect is a slot it never reaches. The ladder's warning about rung 2 is that registration proves presence not reachability, for ACCESS-PATH defects; this is not one. WHAT A RUNG-2 WITNESS WOULD NOT SETTLE, said plainly: it observes the priority TABLE, not delivery. It cannot show that an asserted line 15 is dropped -- for that the carrier's free-running shape is required (sr=0x40000000, vbr into RAM, `bra .` after the trigger, breakpoint at VBR+0x600), and driving a PCIC line needs a PCI device landing on line 15, since dev_sh4.c:2951-2967 registers the 16 lines as `<path>.pcic.<i>` for bus_pci_init's pciirq rather than as anything a guest store reaches directly. So the honest split is: the priority-0 STATE is witnessable at rung 2 today; the DROPPED-DELIVERY symptom is not, and the round should not claim it is. STALE CITATION CORRECTED: the row cites dev_sh4.c:2822-2836 for the wiring; that range is now the default arm's fatal()/exit block. The wiring is at :2951-2967."
