17794-   "state_note": "*** FIRST EVIDENCE 2026-08-27. The row was a BARE TITLE with an empty note; a farmed codex job established it and every load-bearing claim was re-verified here by reading. ***\n\n**THE CLAIM IS TRUE.** `dev_sh4.c` registers SIXTEEN PCIC interrupts (the *'Register 16 PCIC interrupts'* loop over `N_PCIC_IRQS`), and `SH4_INTEVT_IRQ15` is `0x3e0` (`sh4_exception.h:157`). But priority initialisation in `cpu_sh.c` runs\n\n    for (i = SH4_INTEVT_IRQ0; i <= SH4_INTEVT_IRQ14; i += 0x20)\n\n**-- it stops at IRQ14.** Line 15 therefore keeps priority 0, and an assertion at priority 0 returns without scheduling delivery. **A line the device registers can never be delivered.**\n\n**IT IS LATENT, and the seat established that rather than asserting it:** PCIC MMIO never generates an interrupt; no modelled device connects to `.pcic.15`; landisk's only prospective PCI device is compile-disabled AND would use line 5 anyway. **There is no guest access sequence in the shipped tree**, so this ranks below anything guest-reachable.\n\n**THE OBSERVABLE a detector would key on:** guest interrupt-vector entry with `SH4_INTEVT == 0x3e0` -- delivery sets INTEVT and transfers to `VBR+0x600`; the broken code never reaches that handler. That is one channel, not a design.\n\n*The seat labelled its own work honestly: 'MEASURED -- Not run; no build is needed to settle these source facts.' Correct, and it is why this row could be settled under the machine embargo.*\n\n*** ONE VERIFICATION NOTE, because it cuts against my own checking rather than the seat's: my grep for the literal `0x3e0` in the device file returned NOTHING and I nearly scored the citation as wrong. The file uses the SYMBOL `SH4_INTEVT_IRQ15`. The seat cited the right site; my pattern could not see it. Same shape as the other apparatus misses today -- searching for a value where the code names a constant.***\n\nNOT FIXED: extending the loop to IRQ15 is a one-token change, but it is an EDIT TO INTERRUPT PRIORITY INITIALISATION and the addition licence wants a measured delta. With no device on line 15 there is nothing to measure today -- which is precisely why the row is latent, and why the fix should ride with the round that first connects a device there.\n\n"
