19665-   "hold_question": "\n\n*** RE-PIN DEPENDENCY, exported here 2026-08-26 from `gdrompionull` by adjudication -- CLOSURE-GATING, not start-gating. ***\nDe-fatalising the three command-layer exits DESTROYS `gdrompionull`'s detector oracle. That detector's discriminating power is the DEATH MODE (`sig11` vs `exit1` vs `exit0`): a probe CODING ERROR currently lands on `exit1` and is therefore distinguishable from the `sig11` defect. Verified by reading -- the three sites are exactly the ones this row's own census names:\n    :340  TOC `d->cnt != 408`\n    :392  `cmd[1]` not in {0x20,0x24} -- 'unimplemented data format'\n    :470  `default:` -- 'unimplemented command'\nOnce these survive, a mis-encoded probe falls through instead of dying, and a coding error becomes INDISTINGUISHABLE from the defect.\n**`gdromexitsix` MUST NOT CLOSE without re-pinning `gdrompionull`'s detector, and the ORACLE-CORRECTION ORDER is baked in so the re-pin cannot become laundering: re-pin the affected oracles FIRST, measure the pre-de-fatalisation build RED under the new pins, THEN de-fatalise.**\n*Recorded HERE rather than in `gdrompionull`'s prose because the LATER round breaks the EARLIER round's detector -- the obligation must sit where the round that will trip it will see it. This row was assessed 2026-08-23 and `gdrompionull`'s discovery is 2026-08-24, so nothing here mentioned it. Closed-round prose is the exact carrier this project has watched fail.*",
19666-   "sev": "high",
19667-   "note": "*** CLOSED 2026-08-30, RECORDS ONLY.  THE TITLE'S PRESENT TENSE IS HISTORICAL: at HEAD nothing here ends the host. ***  The title is deliberately NOT rewritten -- titles are identity strings other records grep, and precedent on four closed rows (`sh4gdromexit`, `gdromdefault`, `gdromdmadefault`, `lethalonly`) is that none was re-titled at closure.  DISPOSITION OF THE SIX, verified by opening the file rather than reading the filing: `#489` (095aa96) fixed the TOC-length kill; `#490` (fb0cc78) the unimplemented data format and the default unknown command; `#462` (7c9dd9e) both DMA sites, whose primary carriers are the closed rows `gdromdmadefault` and `lethalonly`; and `:1055` is unreachable.  *** THE COMMITS FIELD NAMED ONLY THE FILING COMMIT, AND TWO WHOLE FIX ROUNDS WERE UNATTRIBUTED ANYWHERE IN THE LEDGER. ***  A full-ledger grep found `095aa96` and `fb0cc78` in ZERO rows' commits fields -- this row's own two fix rounds, whose panels sit in this row's entries.  Now `80700b3 7c9dd9e 095aa96 fb0cc78`, which makes the field a complete site-disposition census.  *** THE ABSENCE RECORD FOR `:1055`, WITH ITS WARRANT -- AND THE LEG THAT MAKES IT FUTURE-EDIT-PROOF, WHICH THE FIRST VERSION LEFT IMPLICIT. ***  `cmd_count` has exactly three writers: `:1058/:1059` step it by 2 (narrow access is coerced to 16-bit upstream), `:1147` resets it on 0xa0, and the construction memset.  The `== 12` equality at `:1060` clears `busy & 0x08` synchronously at the boundary, so `>= 12` with the busy bit set has no path.  **THE ADDED LEG: `:917` is `d->busy &= ~idata` -- WRITE-TO-CLEAR ONLY -- and nothing at `:1060-1062` resets `cmd_count`, so it RESTS AT 12 after every completed packet.**  The disagreeing half-state is therefore the device's RESTING state, and unreachability rests entirely on *no path ever SETS `busy & 0x08` except `:1147`'s reset*.  **THAT IS THE RE-RUN TRIGGER**: any future busy-setter -- making `:917` a full write, or a fidelity edit setting busy in reply, which this file's own comment describes mainline hardware doing -- makes the very next data write hit `>= 12` and reach the `exit(1)`.  An absence record must name its warrant, and any edit touching that warrant re-runs the death measurement.  *** THE `hold_question`'s RE-PIN OBLIGATION IS DISCHARGED ***, cited so a closed row does not carry live-looking MUST-NOT-CLOSE text: the challenge set was frozen pre-edit (`challenge_freeze_20260828/`) and measured DISCRIMINATING -- C0 58/58 against C1/C2 55/58, three named rows flipping -- so a probe coding error stays distinguishable from the defect without death modes.  *One wording repair also owed and made: the record said the toclen witness is 'registered CLASS_WITNESS', naming a registry that does not exist -- a grep finds the term only in one gate comment and one brief.  It is MARKED so in a comment, and deliberately ungated because gating a pre-fix-symptom witness manufactures a regression.  A registry with one member is machinery nobody needs.*  *** THE COMMITS GAP WAS BIGGER THAN THE REGRESS REVIEW FOUND, AND THE GATE NAMED THE MISSING ONES EXACTLY. ***  The review restored the three FIX rounds; closing the row then made the attribution check demand FIVE MORE -- `38b07dc`, `c2249eb`, `42d5ee5`, `c43ce97`, `eae8c8c` -- **every one of them literally TITLED `gdromexitsix`**, i.e. this row's own R2 round work.  A field that held ONE commit now holds NINE.  *Twenty-two commits MENTION this row; only nine touched its code, and the check names precisely those, so the set is derivable rather than guessed.  That is the difference between a mention and an attribution, and it is why the field could drift so far without anyone noticing: the row was never closed, so nothing ever asked.*  **The attribution rule only fires at CLOSURE** -- which means an open row can accumulate years of unattributed work in silence.  Fourth firing today, and by some distance the largest."
