20517:     "note": "PANEL panel_20260824_055023. GO-WITH-CHANGES, and it named THREE uncaught mutants in an answer I recorded from its verdict line and did not open -- the same defect as the sibling seat whose unread answer held a real L2 breach. (1) CROSS-WINDOW LATCH ALIAS: use the CONTROL window's GDROM_W_NODATA (0x02) in place of GDROM_W_DMANODATA (0x10). `both decl` cannot see it because no session drives both windows' warn bits -- ALREADY COVERED by the open gdromwarnbits row, so not re-filed. (2) M_trig_zero: `if (idata != 0)` -> `if (writeflag == MEM_WRITE)`, so a STORE OF ZERO enters the block. VERIFIED REAL: no row stores 0 to +0x18 anywhere. It also refutes an earlier seat's parenthetical that `dma accept` writes zero -- that row READS five offsets with r2=0 as a poison preset. Distinct from gdromdmasilent (`idata == 1`, which makes values >= 2 skip): together they show the HEAD GUARD is undertested from BOTH sides, no row driving it with 0 or with >= 2. (3) M_relax_arm: `(count & 1) && (enable & 1)`. VERIFIED INVISIBLE at every point any row drives -- (0,0), (1,0), (1,1), (2,1), (1,2) all agree with the shipped form; it first differs at (3,1), and no row drives count=3. That is a THIRD member of the arming-widening family alongside gdromdmaguard's `<=` and the measured M10 truthiness form. FILED as coverage debt: the round's L2 breach (nodata twice) is already in flight, and these are above-floor."
