30655:   "state_note": "Derived 2026-09-07 while trying to obey the standing directive *prioritise critical bugs and also\neasy resolvable ones*.  **The directive is unexecutable over half the queue.**\n\n    open + in-work        187\n    carrying `sev`        100   (high 10, med 40, low 50)\n    UNRATED                87   = 47%\n    unrated AND WITNESSED  73\n\n**The 73 is the number that matters.**  A witness makes a row ELIGIBLE under the ladder, so those are\nrows that could be worked today and that nothing has ranked.  Ranking is what the carrier says orders\nthe queue -- *rung is a floor on admissibility, never a priority; SEVERITY and gate blind-spots order\nthe queue* -- so an unranked witnessed row is invisible to the only ordering rule this project has.\n\n*** THE FIX IS NOT A REGEX, AND I NEARLY SHIPPED ONE. ***  A keyword scan over titles buckets 7 rows\nunder host-kill language, 5 under memory-safety and 17 under wrong-data.  **Those buckets are\nCORRELATES.**  What makes a row HIGH here is *a guest can reach it and something bad happens*, and no\nkeyword tests reachability -- which is the deriver rule (*key on what DEFINES the class, not on a\ncorrelate of it*) applied to my own triage script.  The scan is kept only as a READING ORDER.\n\n**Candidates the scan surfaced, recorded as UNVERIFIED reading order and explicitly NOT as gradings:**\n`gdromcondavail` (COND_DATA_AVAIL permanently lies after an overread), `asicindexcase` (a deleted\nguard that was also a bounds check), `gdrompiooddlen` (guards one byte, reads two), `asickillsurvive`\n(four kill rows survive-only, so an OOB read is unobserved), `gdromdmawidth` (a tail store ignoring\n`len`), `sh4pcic15` (an interrupt line that can never be delivered), `asicpermute` (an index\npermutation).  **Each needs its reachability read before any `sev` is written.**\n\n> **DISPOSITION: a RATING pass, evidence-first, one row at a time, with the reachability sentence\n> quoted from the source.**  It is read-only, so it parallelises freely and belongs to the file-reading\n> seats -- the exact work the standing directive says to give codex.  It is NOT a round: nothing is\n> edited, and the deliverable is `sev` plus a one-line warrant per row.\n\n*Related but distinct from [[baretitle]], which counts rows with an EMPTY NOTE.  A row can be richly\ndocumented and still unranked -- most of these 73 are.*"
30656-  },
30657-  {
30658-   "id": "randompixdiagonce",
30659-   "sev": "med",
30660-   "state": "open",
30661-   "opened": "2026-09-07",
30662-   "title": "sgi_re_randompixel_probe.py's `lin_b diag once' row does not assert `(once)' -- removing the suppression marker alone leaves it green",
/*
