                            "date":  "2026-08-23",
                            "note":  "dev_sh4.c:2386-2388 refuses ICR IRLM=1 with a once-per-bit diagnostic. #458 links the two decisions in comments at BOTH sites because they are one decision in two files: implementing IRLM=1 makes declining IPRD wrong on the same day, and would need IPRD applied GATED ON THE LIVE IRLM BIT with an explicit policy for the IRQ2/5/8/11 aliasing (do those slots become the IRL pins, or coexist?). *** REOPEN TRIPWIRE FOR sh4iprbcd: if this lands, `iprd hold` flips from DEFENDING the decline to BLOCKING the feature, so its oracle must be re-pinned FIRST under the oracle-correction rule. *** Chip scope matters: IPRD is SH7750S/SH7750R only (Rev.7.00 note 3 at :39881 and :40248), and machine_dreamcast.c:165 asks for plain SH7750 where the register does not exist; :39956-39959 says IRL levels are FIXED on the SH7750 even in IRLM=1. Nothing mechanical enforces the cross-file coupling -- if IRLM=1 is implemented, no test fails."
                        }
                    ]
    },
    {
        "id":  "sh4testclock",
        "title":  "sh4testclock  baresh and testsh have no pclock, so the harness cannot test the TMU path #459 just de-fatalised",
        "state":  "open",
        "commits":  "",
        "hold":  "",
