                            "note":  "SPLIT OUT of gdromcondlies, which named two defects at once. Original record at OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md:7575-7587, a residual of #460: once a guest reads past the buffer, COND_DATA_AVAIL stays SET while every subsequent read returns 0xffff, announced once. Pre-fix that inconsistency was unmissable because the same read ended the host -- so the de-escalation made the state defect QUIETER without removing it, which is the class de-escalation always creates. Clearing COND_DATA_AVAIL at exhaustion would repair it, and was deliberately out of scope for #460 because changing what a device ADVERTISES is a behaviour change with its own oracle. Does NOT join the BADVAL round: different class, different oracle, different fix design."
