    #481 wdc: the reset bit was the head-count bit
    
    src/devices/dev_wdc.c -- the Device Control write arm was four lines:
    
        if (idata & WDCTL_4BIT)
                d->cur_command = COMMAND_RESET;
    
    WDCTL_4BIT is 0x08, "use four head bits (wd1003)" -- which Linux libata holds as its
    STEADY-STATE ap->ctl.  The reset bit is WDCTL_RST, 0x04.  Three measured defects:
    
      * a real soft reset was MISSED.  Older OpenBSD asserts with 0x06 (bit 3 CLEAR)
      * a ROUTINE control write DESTROYED THE RECORD OF WHICH COMMAND IS EXECUTING --
        measured `0xec -> 0x100`.  cur_command is also the value assigned into
        write_in_progress, harmless today ONLY because wdc__write() has one caller
        immediately after the assignment.  An accident, not an invariant
      * an nIEN write latched a reset.  0x0a is libata's polled-mode staple
    
    And the latch is not a reset ACTION: its only readers are the two cylinder-register
    arms, both returning the ATAPI signature 0xEB14 for a CD-ROM.  IT IS THE SIGNATURE
    LATCH -- which is why the wrong bit survived, since triggering on libata's steady
    state kept the signature on almost always.
    
    SHIPPED: WDCTL_RST, LEVEL-triggered, calling #479's helper (forward-declared).
    
    ---- test-first, with an oracle correction inside it ---------------------------
    
    PREFIX_committed_device.out  96 rows 5 failures
    base.out                     96 rows 0 failures     same scripts, opposite colour
    
    One row was RE-PINNED BEFORE THE CODE CHANGED.  It read `cur_command != COMMAND_RESET`,
    conflating "this write did not latch" with "the device is not latched" -- and a seat
    MEASURED the old form going RED on CORRECT code once a power-on signature is modelled.
    
    ---- KILL TABLE 10 of 10, four sole carriers, gate PASS (314 checks) ------------
    
      Mb_revert (b) 5 | Md_nohelper (d) 1 SOLE | Md_nolatch 3 | Md_widemask 1 SOLE
      Md_bitswap 8   | Md_qualcmd 4 | Mo_nienzero 1 SOLE | Mo_nien4bit 2
      Mo_sigalways 1 SOLE | Mc_null COMPILE FAILURE (clause c)
    
    *** Md_bitswap IS CAUGHT BY FOUR ROWS THIS ROUND DID NOT WRITE. ***  #479/#480 shipped
    them saying "built for a fix that has not shipped yet".  THIS IS THAT FIX.  They are
    GREEN on the shipped tree and RED under Md_bitswap -- the same extension WITHOUT the
    bit correction -- so they MEASURED the ordering argument rather than asserting it.
    
    ---- THE PANEL MEASURED MY OWN WARRANT FALSE, and that is the round's L4 ---------
    
    The shipped comment said edge and level are "indistinguishable here", on a
    byte-identical scenario differential.  A seat built the discriminating case using
    REGISTER WRITES ONLY:
    
        assert 0x0e -> 8 guest stores to DATA -> rewrite 0x0e -> release
          LEVEL (shipped):  occ 0, DRQ 0    the ring is purged
          EDGE:             occ 8, DRQ 1    the bytes survive the entire reset
        LIVENESS: same traffic, no reset -> occ 8
        SINGLE ASSERT:                   -> occ 8 BOTH   <- why the round saw no delta
    
    THE ROUND'S DIFFERENTIAL ONLY EVER ASSERTED SRST ONCE.  The decision stands and its
    warrant is now STRONGER -- the measurable difference FAVOURS level.  Two supporting
    claims also failed: idempotence of the helper does NOT licence the inference (it means
    repeating is harmless, not that SKIPPING the repeat is), and the scenario ISSUES NO
    COMMAND, so "no protocol-following driver issues commands while holding SRST" never
    reached it.  Corrected in place.
    
    ---- eighteen escapes measured; three closed in-round, thirteen filed -----------
    
    Two row repairs, both measured by the panel BEFORE they were built:
      * the nIEN row's oracle was ABSOLUTE where its sibling is a DELTA.  A mutant
        clobbering cur_command on an nIEN write -- THE ROUND'S OWN DEFECT #2 through a
        different bit -- walked straight through and the row reported ok
      * the signature rows never pinned the RESET CONJUNCT; the pre-existing control tests
        the other half of that guard
      * plus grok's 0x0c read, which REPAIRS A FALSE CLAIM BY MAKING IT TRUE
    
    ROOT CAUSE is how a row was CUT: the sole-carrier abort row sets writer, ATAPI flag,
    phase and ring SIMULTANEOUSLY, so it cannot distinguish which gates the abort.  And
    altctl_fresh() pins five stub defaults in which SIX of the eighteen escapes live --
    a fresh instance of "A STUB'S DEFAULT VALUE IS AN UNTESTED BRANCH SELECTOR", written
    down in this tree four hours earlier.
    
    ---- THIS ROUND IS RUNG 3, NOT RUNG 1 -------------------------------------------
    
    The lifecycle ask -- before recording a round rung-1, ask ONE seat to try a rung-3
    probe -- PAID OFF THE FIRST TIME IT WAS MADE.  One invocation built it on unmodified
    `evbmips -e malta`: symptom on pre-fix HEAD, green post-fix with the same script,
    LIVENESS (0x55/0x66 written and read back through the same decode) and
    DEVICE-SIGNATURE (0xeb14 is a value the guest never wrote) controls.
    
    ---- "FILED" HAD SHIPPED AHEAD OF THE FILING ------------------------------------
    
    wdcponsig was asserted "filed with measurements" in TWO commit-bound artifacts while
    appearing in ZERO queue files.  The pending docs step is ordinary; the past tense
    running ahead of the action is not.  Filed properly here, with wdcaltctrlcov (the 13
    escapes), wdcresetirq, and wdcaltdecode.
    
    wdcaltdecode is the one to read: three decode paths into the control register that no
    row covers, and THE FIX ENLARGES ALL THREE -- it converts a benign signature-latch
    toggle into a destructive state abort.  Pre-existing, not introduced, filed with its
    rung-3 measurements.
    
    ---- the weekly battery was RED for 91 hours, fixed here ------------------------
    
    gate_build failed `no stale allowlist entries got=1 want=0`, and gate_mips then SKIPPED
    as a consequence -- the documented silent-coverage-loss shape.  Cause: arcbios.c no
    longer diverges.  THE DANGEROUS READING WAS CHECKED FIRST -- both trees carry the same
    ten fork tags, so no hardening was lost.  The entry lived in TWO files with different
    path conventions; fixing one would have left the gate red.
    
    ---- five record corrections, and three are the same class ----------------------
    
    Comments that were TRUE WHEN WRITTEN and that this round falsified by changing the code
    they describe: #479's helper header (four present-tense claims, two callers now),
    #477's accept-row premise, #480's not-yet-shipped prediction.  I corrected the instance
    at the arm and left its siblings sixty lines above -- mechanical rule 2 exactly.
    
    Plus: "both carry bit 3" (0x02 & 0x08 == 0, and the round's own pre-fix log says so),
    and a signature header claiming a power-on row that does not exist.
    
    Gate: offline-differential PASS (314 checks), 96 rows 0 failures.  precommit
    PRECOMMIT_PASS 0 hard.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

